members.doc:
Two steps on purpose. Naming what WOULD be cooked is a string lookup;
producing the geometry is a copy of the whole mesh. Splitting them means
the hundredth instance of a prop pays the string and stops there.

Call on module unload. The resolver is code inside the installing image;
leaving the pointer behind after that image goes away is a call into
freed memory the next time a mesh collider spawns.

p.AsyncTick: fixed steps this Update handed to a worker and has not yet
joined. Non-zero between one Update's return and the next one's start;
every PhysicsWorld entry point that reaches Jolt joins on its own.
